# - resource -------------------------------------------------------------------

<https://YasniiSS.github.io/fhir4eyes/ValueSet/binocular-finding-vs> a fhir:ValueSet ;
  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:Resource.id [ fhir:value "binocular-finding-vs"] ;
  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "extensions" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: ValueSet binocular-finding-vs</b></p><a name=\"binocular-finding-vs\"> </a><a name=\"hcbinocular-finding-vs\"> </a><p>This value set includes codes based on the following rules:</p><ul><li>Include these codes as defined in <a href=\"CodeSystem-fhir4eyes-cs.html\"><code>https://YasniiSS.github.io/fhir4eyes/CodeSystem/fhir4eyes-cs</code></a><span title=\"Version is not explicitly stated, which means it is fixed to the version provided in this specification\"> version ?0.4.0</span><table class=\"none\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-fhir4eyes-cs.html#fhir4eyes-cs-fusion\">fusion</a></td><td>Fusion</td><td>Sensory fusion: the images of both eyes are combined into a single percept (e.g. a single pinkish light on the red filter plus light test, four lights on the Worth 4 dot test). SNOMED CT 78513008 Fusion binocular vision is an observable entity, not a finding, so it is not used as an answer.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-fhir4eyes-cs.html#fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-reflex-centered\">corneal-reflex-centered</a></td><td>Corneal light reflex centered</td><td>On corneal light reflex (Hirschberg) testing, the reflex is centered on the pupil of the eye assessed, consistent with no manifest deviation of that eye.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-fhir4eyes-cs.html#fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-reflex-displaced-nasal\">corneal-reflex-displaced-nasal</a></td><td>Corneal light reflex displaced nasally</td><td>On corneal light reflex (Hirschberg) testing, the reflex in the eye assessed is displaced nasally from the pupil centre, indicating an exodeviation of that eye.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-fhir4eyes-cs.html#fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-reflex-displaced-temporal\">corneal-reflex-displaced-temporal</a></td><td>Corneal light reflex displaced temporally</td><td>On corneal light reflex (Hirschberg) testing, the reflex in the eye assessed is displaced temporally from the pupil centre, indicating an esodeviation of that eye.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-fhir4eyes-cs.html#fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-reflex-displaced-superior\">corneal-reflex-displaced-superior</a></td><td>Corneal light reflex displaced superiorly</td><td>On corneal light reflex (Hirschberg) testing, the reflex in the eye assessed is displaced superiorly from the pupil centre, indicating a hypodeviation of that eye.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-fhir4eyes-cs.html#fhir4eyes-cs-corneal-reflex-displaced-inferior\">corneal-reflex-displaced-inferior</a></td><td>Corneal light reflex displaced inferiorly</td><td>On corneal light reflex (Hirschberg) testing, the reflex in the eye assessed is displaced inferiorly from the pupil centre, indicating a hyperdeviation of that eye.</td></tr></table></li><li>Include these codes as defined in <a href=\"http://www.snomed.org/\"><code>http://snomed.info/sct</code></a><span title=\"Version is not explicitly stated. No matching Code System found\"> version Not Stated (use latest from terminology server)</span><table class=\"none\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://snomed.info/id/1052232003\">1052232003</a></td><td>Suppression of visual signal of right eye</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://snomed.info/id/1052231005\">1052231005</a></td><td>Suppression of visual signal of left eye</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://snomed.info/id/251756006\">251756006</a></td><td>Heteronymous diplopia</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"http://snomed.info/id/251755005\">251755005</a></td><td>Homonymous diplopia</td></tr></table></li></ul></div>"
  ] ;
